* The look of SimpleWiki (the **shell**) is kept by MWS as a template with numbered **releases**.

* A wiki follows its template under a **shell policy**: `auto` always takes the newest, `notify` stays and asks first, `pin` stays on one release. New wikis start with `notify`.
* Under `notify`, a newer release shows a sign to the **owner and the administrators**: a dot on the gear and, in the Settings dialog, a button **"Adopt"**. It calls `PUT /recipe/<slug>/shell/update`, the server moves the wiki to the new release and reloads it.
* **The contents of your wiki are not changed!** You can dismiss the hint (until the next offered version or for a month).
* Whoever may only write does not see the hint — adopting a shell is an owner decision.